# MASTER PROJECT PROMPT: NURZAM’S LIBRARY

## 1. Project Overview

Build a complete, responsive, public-facing personal book library website called **Nurzam’s Library**.

The website will serve as a digital catalogue of my personal reading collection. Visitors can explore my books, discover what I am currently reading, browse completed books, view my wishlist, explore authors and genres, and follow my reading history and statistics.

The website must use **Notion as the single source of truth for all book data**. I will manage, add, edit, and delete books exclusively through my Notion database. The website must automatically retrieve and publish the latest data from Notion every 30 minutes.

The project must be lightweight, maintainable, inexpensive to host, and suitable for deployment through GitHub Pages.

### Core principles

1. Notion is the only content-management interface.
2. The website is publicly accessible and read-only.
3. Book data synchronises automatically every 30 minutes.
4. Use HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript for the frontend.
5. Use GitHub Actions for scheduled Notion synchronisation.
6. Host the website using GitHub Pages.
7. Follow a distinctive **Playful Neo-Brutalist design system**.
8. Prioritise usability, readability, performance, accessibility, and responsive behaviour.
9. Avoid unnecessary frameworks, dependencies, services, and infrastructure.

