## 3. System Architecture

Implement the following architecture:

```text
                    NOTION
              (Book Database)
                     |
                     |
                Notion API
                     |
                     v
              GITHUB ACTIONS
             (Every 30 Minutes)
                     |
          Fetch and transform data
                     |
          Validate and sanitise data
                     |
                     v
               library.json
                     |
                     |
                GITHUB PAGES
                     |
                     v
             NURZAM'S LIBRARY
              Public Website
```

### How it works

1. I manage my books inside Notion.
2. GitHub Actions runs automatically every 30 minutes.
3. The synchronisation script retrieves the latest database records using the Notion API.
4. It transforms Notion properties into a consistent public JSON structure.
5. It validates the data and excludes any fields that should not be publicly exposed.
6. It generates or updates the public JSON data.
7. GitHub Pages serves the updated website and library data.

### Important implementation requirements

- The Notion integration token must never appear in frontend JavaScript, HTML, CSS, or publicly accessible JSON.
- Store the Notion integration token in GitHub Secrets.
- Store the Notion database ID in GitHub Secrets or repository configuration.
- Do not expose private Notion properties.
- Do not make the public website depend on direct Notion API requests.
- Avoid committing secrets or credentials.
- Avoid unnecessary commits when the generated library data has not changed.
- Handle Notion API pagination correctly.
- Handle API rate limits, transient errors, and failed synchronisation gracefully.
- Do not overwrite valid published data with an empty or incomplete result caused by an API failure.
- Preserve the last successfully generated JSON if synchronisation fails.
- Log synchronisation results and errors in GitHub Actions.

### Synchronisation frequency

Configure GitHub Actions to run every 10 minutes:

```yaml
schedule:
  - cron: "*/10 * * * *"
```

Also support manual execution through `workflow_dispatch`.

GitHub Actions scheduled workflows can be delayed occasionally. Do not promise exact real-time synchronisation at precisely 30-minute intervals.

