### 6.2 To Read

Display books that have the To Be Read status.

This page should help me discover what to read next.

Include:

**A. AI Curated Next Up**

This is an important feature.

Create an automatically generated reading recommendation section that prioritises books based on my reading history and preferences.

The system should consider:

1. Historical ratings.
2. Genre preferences.
3. Author familiarity.
4. Reading length.
5. Reading pace and variety.
6. Previously completed books.
7. Favourite authors or genres, when the data supports them.

The recommendations must be generated automatically.

I do not want to manually rearrange a reading queue or assign a position to every book.

The recommendation engine should calculate a ranking whenever the library data changes or when the website loads.

**Recommended initial implementation:**

Use a transparent, rule-based recommendation algorithm in JavaScript.

Do not require a paid AI API or a continuously running backend.

Suggested scoring logic:

- Genre affinity: prioritise genres associated with my higher-rated completed books.
- Author familiarity: give a modest preference to authors I have previously rated positively.
- Reading-length balance: favour shorter books after completing a particularly long book.
- Reading variety: occasionally recommend books from genres I have not read recently.
- Personal favourites: consider favourite authors and books when those properties exist.

Use a weighted scoring model.

Example conceptual weights:

| Factor | Suggested Weight |
|---|---:|
| Genre affinity | 40% |
| Author familiarity | 20% |
| Reading-length balance | 20% |
| Reading variety | 15% |
| Other relevant preferences | 5% |

These weights should be configurable in the recommendation module.

Do not fabricate reading preferences when insufficient data exists.

When there is not enough reading history, use sensible fallback behaviour:

- Prioritise highly rated books, if ratings exist.
- Otherwise, show a varied selection of To Be Read books.
- Explain that recommendations will improve as more reading history becomes available.

Display a brief explanation of why a book was recommended, such as:

- "Matches your favourite genres."
- "A familiar author."
- "A shorter read after a long book."
- "A chance to explore something different."

Do not claim that this initial rule-based system is using an LLM or performing genuine generative AI reasoning.

Keep the recommendation engine modular so that a real AI provider can be integrated later without rebuilding the website.

