## 11. Statistics and Calculations

All statistics must be calculated from the available book records.

Implement a dedicated statistics module.

Examples:

- Total collection size.
- Number of books read.
- Number of books currently being read.
- Number of books to read.
- Number of wishlist books.
- Number of DNF books.
- Average rating.
- Total pages read.
- Books completed per year.
- Reading format distribution.
- Genre distribution.
- Author distribution.

### Calculation rules

- Only books with status Read count as completed.
- DNF books must not count as completed.
- Wishlist books must not count as To Be Read.
- Do not count missing page counts as zero pages.
- Do not include unrated books in average-rating calculations.
- Do not include invalid or missing dates in date-based statistics.
- Avoid dividing by zero.
- Clearly distinguish an unavailable statistic from a genuine zero.

